========================================================================
SOURCE REVIEW (7.10 — no product edit)
========================================================================

`ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret.oo` (264 lines, ≤600; soft 256 already over
pre-7.10; Domain A did not grow the file):

```
pub fn c_parse_secret_env(src: String) -> String
  needle = "// " + "SECRET:"          // line-start only
  skip " " / "\t" after colon
  start = k
  while is_al: k = k + 1              // NO name = name + c
  name = str_slice(src, start, k)     // ONE slice per directive
  if name == "": ERR invalid name; process_exit(1)
  c_env_put __sec__name=1
  c_env_put __secref__name=1
  i = k                               // next line-start SECRET still seen
```

Static (this peer, after Domain A):

| Grep | Result |
|------|--------|
| `name = name + c` in file | **0** |
| `str_slice` | L65 (OWN) + L254 (`__sec_sink__` prefix — **not** 7.10) |
| empty-name fail-closed | L66–69 unchanged |
| multi-name continue | L73 `i = k` then outer loop |

Ident class is still `_A-Za-z0-9` from the **first** char (leading
digits allowed). That is pre-existing, not a 7.10 rewrite.

Dirty-tree also has 2.10 `__sec_sink__` scan at L253–257. **Not** this
OWN; not re-proved here.

